/-!
# Round six, bit network: the generated chunks of the two stage words

For the stage words `W1F`, `W2F`:
* their gates are the lists `G1`, `G2` of `R6BitNBScalB`;
* every instruction has a valid code, touches local wires (`< NL`) and its gates join distinct
  touched wires;
* the generator, started at the packed states `SG1_0`, `SG2_0`, ends at `SG1_11`, `SG2_10`; all
  its moves are nested (`nestOK`) between valid codes, and the move ranks are counted by the sums
  of the segment counts.

